# {{PRODUCT}} — Gemini CLI / Antigravity

Follow `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md`; the kernel wins.

- Python: `{{PY}}` | Assemble: `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py assemble` | Device: {{DEVICE_POLICY}} | {{GIT_POLICY}}
- Harness Boundary & Incidents: `.agents/**` is immutable; never read or patch `.agents/scripts/**` during app tasks. On traceback or `INCIDENT_RECORDED=<id>`, ask via `ask_question` before `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py report-issue --submit --incident-id <id>`.
- Consultation & Pre-Planning Clarification:
  - Read-only inquiries inspect and answer in chat without `draft` or file edits; discuss requested trade-offs in chat BEFORE `draft`.
  - Before `draft`, clarify missing requirements or hard decisions (Room schema, exported components, permissions, public contracts): ask the developer about it with `ask_question`; for a Room change ask about an existing destructive fallback, users on older schema versions and downgrade first. Carry answers into `--approach` / `--risks` / `--device-strategy` (resolve `PLAN_GAPS=` via `revise`).
- Plan Approval Clarity & Antigravity Planning Lifecycle:
  - The approval question is the request: never add a separate sentence asking for approval.
  - Proceed appears ONLY on initial task approval; execute in-scope follow-ups directly (`task plan-note` before `prepare-verification`). For direct `1–2` primary-file `T0`/`T1` micro-tasks (zero DB/Auth/Billing/Permission/Network/Nav surfaces), use `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task quick-start --outcome "<goal>" --files <paths> --source conversation --proof-reference "<request>"` (auto-falls back to `AWAITING_DEVELOPER_APPROVAL` when `T2+`) and finish in one call via `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task ship --task-id <id> --host antigravity`. On standard chat approval, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task approve --repo . --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>" --enforcement-tier RULE_ENFORCED --plan-hash <hash from PLAN_HASH>`.
- Tool-First & `ask_question` Formatting:
  - Emit `ask_question`, `run_command`, or `invoke_subagent` IMMEDIATELY as your first token after thinking with ZERO pre-tool prose (no `---` dividers or `*(...)*` notes) and NO pipe tables `| ... |` inside `ask_question`. For Plan Approval, follow the `APPROVAL_QUESTION` line (`PLAN_DOCUMENT_URI` link to `plan.md`, then the `APPROVAL_BRIEF` lines translated, each said once, as markdown with bold labels, never in a code block: 2-4 sub-bullets, phases/files `<=3` names, 2-3 phone checks; on revised plans, ask only about the delta); in a right-to-left language, start each line with a word in that language and put code/file/English terms in backticks. Never prefix `(Recommended)` onto device-verdict, plan/sensitive approval, or commit options.
- Shared-Quota Orchestration, Warm-Cache Execution & Anti-Reread:
  - Keep main chat on `Gemini 4 Hydrogen High` (`1.00x`), `Gemini 4 Neon (High)`, `Gemini 4 Carbon (Medium)` (summarize trade-offs in plain text BEFORE tool batches `#200671`), or `Claude Sonnet/Opus 5.5`; NEVER select `Hydrogen Extra`/`xHigh` (`#200467` drains `3x Argon`).
  - **Discovery**: Inspect `1–3` known files inline (`task-context`/`view_file`). To inspect third-party library APIs/KDoc (even before Android Studio Sync), run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py dep-inspect <group:artifact[:version]> --query <symbol>` (never dump bytecode or paginate `build/**`). For `4+` files or unfamiliar flows, invoke `1–3` parallel `TypeName = "harness-scout-agent"`, `Role = "harness-scout-agent"`, `Workspace = "inherit"`, passing `Model = "flash"` unconditionally (routes natively to `gemini-4-hydrogen-tiered-high` `1x` regardless of main-chat model; omit `Model` ONLY when explicit `inherit` is configured, NEVER `research`/`explore`).
  - **Inline Execution (`INLINE_LEAD_DIRECT`)**: Follow `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py delegate-plan --json` — implement production & test edits directly on the warm Lead session with concise English KDoc (`/** ... */`) on new/added contracts, zero unused parameters/functions/classes (`fast_kt_lint` hard-blocks dead intra-file code), and JVM Robolectric/Compose RTL (`ar-rSA-ldrtl`) tests on UI changes when Robolectric/Roborazzi is configured (`test --capture-red` first on `BUG` tasks), then run `checkpoint-phase --advance-all-ready` or `verify-steps`.
  - **Execution Mode & Web-Relay**: Local execution (`normal`) is the default without interrupting the developer; Web-Relay prompting is opt-in (`execution-mode set --choice ask-every-task` or `web-task`). If `SELECT_EXECUTION_MODE_REQUIRED` fires (opt-in `ask-every-task` or explicit `web-pack`), ask via `ask_question` stating approximate quota savings (`~60%-85%`) with the 3 choices (`normal-task`, `web-task`, `normal-project`) and record via `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py execution-mode set --choice <choice> --source conversation --proof-reference "<answer>"`. In `web` mode, pack via `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py web-pack [--task-id <id>] [--file <paths...>] [--prompt "<goal>"] [--feature <name>] [--dirty] [--add-files <paths...>] [--retry | --retry-failure] [--batch-size <N> | --all-in-one]`, instructing the developer to open a **NEW external AI chat** for a new task (same chat only for retries/batches); apply replies via `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py web-apply --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>" [--task-id <id>] [--dry-run] [--staged-phase] [--approve-sensitive] [--file <path>]` with NO `--file` flag first, then run `verify-steps` without re-reading applied files (on multi-line compile/test/gate failure, run `web-pack --task-id <id> --retry-failure` for the SAME chat).
  - **Zero Post-Subagent Re-Read**: Never re-run `graph` or re-read files analyzed by scouts, specialists, or reviewers (`<= 3` surgical `<= 200`-line gap checks).
- Operational Guardrails & Zero-Polling:
  - Cancel is the developer's (`task cancel` only when asked); for `--proof-reference`, never write their reason for them; use `replace_file_content` / `multi_replace_file_content` for existing files; never write transcripts.
  - **Windows Shell, `search_web` (`#201621`) & Subprocess Hygiene (`#200632`/`#200687`/`#201582`)**: Emit standalone single-line commands in `run_command` (no pipes `|`, redirections `>`, `;`/`&&`, or `python -c`); use batched `harness.py` commands and native search/read tools instead of scattered shell commands or `agy` subprocesses; check `.agents/project-context/` before web search and issue at most `1–2` `search_web` calls per turn (never `3+` parallel calls `#201621`); judge compiler truth by on-disk `compile` (`#200619`).
  - **Zero-Polling**: Yield with ZERO tool calls while background tasks/subagents run; never poll `manage_task`, `manage_subagents`, `schedule`, or `.system_generated/tasks/*.log`; reap finished waves via `manage_subagents({"Action": "kill_all"})` AFTER `complete-all` succeeds; self-certification (`record_review.py --verdict PASS`) is forbidden.
- Review Host Binding & Exact Reviewer Dispatch Procedure (Antigravity):
  - Prepare: `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task prepare-verification --repo . --task-id <id> --host antigravity`.
  - On `DISPATCH_REVIEWERS` / `DISPATCH_PHASE_REVIEWERS`: (1) handle `SELECT_REVIEW_MODEL` if present via `ask_question`; (2) invoke every reviewer in parallel via `invoke_subagent` (`TypeName = role`, `Role = role`, `Prompt` = `reviewer_prompts[role]`, `Workspace = inherit`; pass `Model = "flash"` for all `hydrogen`/`flash` reviewers regardless of main-chat model, `Model = "pro"` if `pro`, and omit `Model` (`INHERIT_PARENT_BY_OMISSION`) only for explicit `inherit` or explicit `Carbon`/`Neon`/`Argon`; define from `.agents/subagents/<role>.json` with write/MCP flags `false` if unloaded); (3) print `| Reviewer | Model | Status |` and yield; (4) run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review complete-all --task <id>` (or `phase-review complete-all --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase>`; recover env/protocol blocks via `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task heal --task-id <id>`).
- Mobile Verification Walkthrough: After `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py device install-start` (or `device skip-validation`), invoke `ask_question` IMMEDIATELY with the 3-section **Mobile Verification Walkthrough** before `device signoff`.

